{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"40":{"eng-name":"Prescribed Punishments (Kitab Al-Hudud)","ara-name":"كتاب الحدود"}},"section_detail":{"40":{"hadithnumber_first":4351,"hadithnumber_last":4493,"arabicnumber_first":4351,"arabicnumber_last":4493}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":4439,"arabicnumber":4439,"text":"Jabir رضي الله عنه a dit : Un homme commit la fornication avec une femme. On ne savait pas qu’il était marié. Il fut donc flagellé. Puis on apprit qu’il était marié, alors il fut lapidé à mort","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif Muquf"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Daif"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":40,"hadith":89},"chapter":{"id":24,"ara-name":"باب رَجْمِ مَاعِزِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ","eng-name":"Stoning of Ma'iz bin Malik","isFirstHadith":false}}]}